    "https://cuny.jobs/bronx-ny/assistant-professor-of-political-science-specialization-in-american-politics/7CA71701A90D4FDA8369EDA1FF4F393A/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics Bronx, NY LEHMAN COLLEGE Apply Now Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT Lehman College, of The City University of New York, ranks among the top five institutions in the nation for fostering social mobility. A four-year Hispanic Serving Institution in the Bronx, Lehman offers bachelor’s, master’s, and advanced degrees and certificate programs in the Liberal Arts, sciences, and professions. The College’s community-driven mission and notable academic programs attract a diverse, international enrollment of over 15,000 students who take courses on its 37-acre, tree-lined campus and online degree programs. Many thousands more community members benefit yearly from its active cultural, educational, health, and economic outreach programs and services. The Department of Political Science at Lehman College, The City University of New York, invites applications for an Assistant Professor in American politics, beginning Fall 2027. We welcome applications from scholars across the field, and are especially interested in candidates whose research and teaching engage one or more of the following areas: public law, including constitutional law, law and courts, law and society, and American constitutional development; immigration law, policy, and politics, including citizenship; criminal justice and civil rights; American political behavior and institutions, including elections, public opinion, parties, and political participation; American political development; and the intersection of technology and politics, including artificial intelligence. A central service responsibility for the position will be pre-law advising. The appointee will serve as the department’s pre-law advisor and will lead the pre-law program, departmental internships, and the minor in Law and Government. Candidates must be able to teach the department’s introductory course on American government and politics. Responsibilities of the academic appointment include maintaining an active program of scholarship and a robust publication record; developing courses and curriculum and teaching introductory and advanced undergraduate courses; and service to the department and full participation in the life of the College and the University. Obtaining grant funding to support research and institutional initiatives is encouraged. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills and the ability to work collegially as a team member are also important. The faculty member may have the opportunity to become involved in graduate programs (master’s and PhD level) at the CUNY Graduate Center. The appointment requires regular on-campus presence for teaching, advising, office hours, and departmental and College activities, although some online teaching or remote administrative work may be involved. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Political Science or related field or J.S.D./S.J.D., in hand by start date. Preferred: J.D./Ph.D.; experience with or commitment to pre-law advising and mentoring students toward legal and public careers; a robust record of teaching and research. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. COMPENSATION $98,231 - $112,841 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Applicants should be prepared to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing samples, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g. sample syllabi, summary of teaching evaluations, teaching statement). Letters of recommendation will be requested for candidates advanced to the semi-finalist round. Review of applications will begin in early October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to joseph.mohorcich@lehman.cuny.edu and elhum.haghighat@lehman.cuny.edu. CLOSING DATE Applications to be received until November 2nd, 2026. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32747 Location: Lehman College Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/lecturer-accounting/33A402692C634102827DF08396567999/job/": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Accounting | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Lecturer - Accounting New York, NY BARUCH COLLEGE Apply Now Lecturer - Accounting FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT \"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyone’s responsibility” The Stan Ross Department of Accountancy is seeking applicants for one lecturer position in Accounting starting Fall 2027, subject to final budget approval. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate and graduate courses in accounting. Additionally, the successful candidate is expected to mentor students (undergraduate and master’s students) and undertake significant service to the department. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelors degree plus significant professional experience or Masters degree required in accounting or a related field. Demonstrate an ability and commitment to deliver high-quality teaching in accounting, auditing or taxation. Prior professional work experience in these fields and professional certification (e.g., CPA) are a plus. Successful candidates will be required to participate in Baruch’s “Inclusive Pedagogy” workshop and CUNY’s “Innovative Teaching Academy,” and demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching in a diverse and inclusive environment. Applicants must be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. COMPENSATION $92,359- $106,547; salary commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. To ensure consideration, applications must be received via the official CUNY application system. Candidates should provide a CV/resume. Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. CLOSING DATE December 1, 2026 with review of resumes to begin September 15, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32729 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
