    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/professor-mathematics/899424D3BC19477E90C2FDD081F61160/job/": {
      "title": "Professor",
      "description": "Professor - Mathematics | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Professor - Mathematics New York, NY BARUCH COLLEGE Apply Now Professor - Mathematics FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT \"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyone’s responsibility” Baruch College, located in the historic Gramercy Park/Flatiron district of Manhattan, is one of eleven senior colleges of the City University of New York (CUNY), housing the Weissman School of Arts and Sciences, the Zicklin School of Business, and the Marxe School of Public and International Affairs. We are proud to serve a diverse and engaged student body of over 19,000. Our students represent a wealth of racial, ethnic, economic, religious, linguistic, and national origin backgrounds, and include many recent immigrants as well as individuals who are the first in their families to attend college. Baruch is ranked among the top institutions of higher education in the nation by The Wall Street Journal for promoting student social mobility. Baruch is also listed among the nation’s top public colleges for academic excellence. Baruch seeks staff and faculty members who thrive in multicultural academic environments and are committed to access and excellence in higher education. Visit us at https://www.baruch.cuny.edu/. The Department of Mathematics of Baruch College – CUNY invites applications for an anticipated tenure-track position at full professor rank beginning on or about August 26, 2027. (Immediate tenure eligible only for candidates currently holding tenure at another institution of higher education in the US.) The department is seeking a candidate with at least ten years of experience in the financial sector, a strong publication record in top journals, as well as significant graduate-level teaching experience in financial engineering. The candidate must have a PhD in mathematics, applied mathematics, physics, or a related field and a scholarly record suitable for full professor rank. The department offers a world-renowned masters degree in financial engineering. At the undergraduate level, the department offer majors in financial mathematics, mathematics, actuarial science, and computer science as well as providing general education mathematics courses. QUALIFICATIONS The candidate must have a PhD in mathematics, applied mathematics, physics, or a related field. At least ten years of experience in the financial sector, a strong publication record in top journals, as well as significant graduate-level teaching experience in financial engineering. COMPENSATION $136,040- $160,827; commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. All applications must be submitted online both at Mathjobs.org and at CUNYFirst. A complete application at MathJobs.org will include an AMS cover sheet, curriculum vitae including a list of publications, at least three letters of reference, one of which should address the candidate's teaching, short statements describing teaching philosophy and future research plans. In addition, applicants should submit a narrative statement describing their commitment to working effectively with faculty, staff, and students in a multicultural/multiethnic urban campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. The application at CUNY First will include candidate’s curriculum vitae, answers to screening and self identification questions, and an agreement to terms and conditions. Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered. If you have any questions, please contact HR at 646-660-6590. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: AMS Cover sheet Curriculum Vitae (including a list of publications) Research Statement Teaching Statement Multicultural Statement Three or More Reference Letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on Mathjobs.org) and anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: http://www.baruch.cuny.edu/math/ Prof. Warren Gordon Baruch College One Bernard Baruch Way, Box B6-230 New York, NY 10010 CLOSING DATE November 1, 2026 with review of resumes to begin October 1, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32733 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/associate-professor-of-philosophy-arthur-zitrin-professorship-in-bioethics/1FE0AF63289849998A49A1438CF83EC6/job/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Associate Professor of Philosophy - Arthur Zitrin Professorship in Bioethics | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Associate Professor of Philosophy - Arthur Zitrin Professorship in Bioethics New York, NY CITY COLLEGE OF NEW YORK Apply Now Associate Professor of Philosophy - Arthur Zitrin Professorship in Bioethics FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT About the City College of New York For over 175 years, The City College of New York has provided access to high-quality education for New Yorkers in a wide variety of disciplines. Over 13,000 students pursue undergraduate and graduate degrees in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, the School of Architecture, the School of Education, the Grove School of Engineering, the Center for Worker Education, the Colin Powell School for Civic and Global Leadership, and the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education. The City College of New York has produced ten Nobel laureates. About the City College of New York Philosophy Department The Philosophy Department has nine full-time faculty members, 100 majors and 60 minors, an active Philosophy Club, and frequent departmental events, including the Philosophy Pizza Forum. Position Details The Department of Philosophy at The City College of New York (CCNY) of the City University of New York (CUNY) invites applications for the Arthur Zitrin Professorship in Bioethics, an endowed position to be filled at the rank of Associate Professor, anticipated to begin in Fall 2027. The position will involve research, undergraduate teaching at the introductory level and in the applicant’s areas of expertise, and departmental service. The Zitrin Professorship will provide support of $10,000-$40,000 in addition to the salary range specified below, depending on experience and qualifications. Area of Specialization: Bioethics Area of Competence: Open QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. degree in Philosophy. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of excellence in research, teaching, and departmental service. Preferred but not required: experience in administering programs for students, such as internships, and/or experience with grants that could support such programs. COMPENSATION Salary Range: $94,017 - $113,745 The Zitrin Professorship will provide support of $10,000-$40,000 in addition to the salary range, depending on experience and qualifications. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Only applications submitted through CUNYfirst will be considered for this position. If you are viewing this job posting in CUNYfirst, please click on \"Apply Now\" on the bottom of this page and follow the instructions. If you are viewing this job posting externally, please apply as follows: Go to https://cuny.jobs/ Search for Job Opening ID number 32774 Click on the \"Apply Now\" button and follow the instructions. Applications, including the following, must be uploaded to the CUNYfirst job application website as a single PDF document: Cover Letter; Curriculum Vitae Summaries of recent student teaching evaluations; At least one article-length writing sample, and no more than three; Contact information (including email address) for at least three people willing to provide letters of recommendation. CLOSING DATE November 15, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32774 Location: City College of New York Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-tenure-track-or-tenure-architecture-and-urban-ai/C09D3C2DFF604DD0BA1D17AF434888B2/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (Tenure-track or Tenure)",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (Tenure-track or Tenure) - Architecture and Urban AI | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (Tenure-track or Tenure) - Architecture and Urban AI New York, NY CITY COLLEGE OF NEW YORK Apply Now Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (Tenure-track or Tenure) - Architecture and Urban AI FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT The Bernard and Anne Spitzer School of Architecture at the City College of New York is pleased to announce a faculty search as part of the CUNY Martin S. Spergel Initiative in Computational Science supported by the Simons Foundation. The Spitzer School seeks colleague, preferably mid to senior career who will take a leading role in defining the interdisciplinary Spergel cluster, Urban AI: Intelligent Systems for Sustainability and Planning in Urban Settings. The field of specialty for this full-time tenured or tenure-track position is artificial intelligence and physical design in the urban built environment, engaging emerging fields such as geospatial AI, cyber-physical systems, robotics, or physical AI. This faculty appointment will commence in Fall 2027 and includes teaching, research, and service responsibilities allied with Spitzer’s undergraduate and graduate programs in architecture, landscape architecture, urban design, and urban studies along with teaching responsibility in the CUNY Graduate Center. Through the Martin S. Spergel Initiative in Computational Sciences, the position carries a substantial startup package. We seek a cutting-edge, imaginative scholar whose research builds new computational methods, tools, and theories for design, who understands AI as a creative force in shaping the built environment, and who grapples with the ethical questions that AI raises. The successful candidate will direct this work toward urgent urban challenges, including sustainability, climate resilience, and social equity. As an intellectual leader of the Urban AI cluster, this person will develop, define, and shape its research and pedagogical agendas, and shape the long-term vision of the initiative in partnership with colleagues at the Spitzer School, the City College of New York, Queens College, and the CUNY Graduate Center. Although interdisciplinary collaboration is expected, this position is seated in the architecture department at the Spitzer School. A dedicated teacher is needed who is committed to teaching artificial intelligence and computational methods to design students at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The appointee will also contribute to the MS in Computational Sciences at the CUNY Graduate Center. The successful candidate will join a vibrant research community at the Spitzer School, one that is supported by City Labs, a consortium made up of the Robotics Laboratory with industrial robots, the Advanced Building Construction Laboratory, focused on decarbonization, and the Living Systems Laboratory. The J. Max Bond Center for Urban Futures offers further expertise in urban data analytics with a focus on community engagement. The Spitzer School is committed to social and sustainable concerns in design and practice, as well as to providing access to the finest education in the art, history, and technology of architecture, landscape architecture, urban design, and urban studies to the broadest and most diverse student population. A prospective member of the faculty should be prepared to participate in and contribute to this lively intellectual atmosphere and join the SSA in its commitment in furthering justice, equity, diversity, and inclusion within the academy and the design professions. Expect to share responsibility for committee and department assignments including administrative, supervisory, and other functions. QUALIFICATIONS For Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor: Ph.D. degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Preferred Qualifications A PhD in architecture, design computation, planning, or a closely related field and a terminal degree in design (architecture or landscape architecture). Completion of the PhD is required before the start date in late August 2027. A demonstrated research agenda applying artificial intelligence or computational methods to design and the urban built environment. A record of teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in design studios, seminars, and/or lecture courses, including the ability to teach AI and computational methods to design students. A sustained record of research, publication, and external funding sufficient for appointment at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor. Expertise in one or more emerging areas such as geospatial AI, cyber-physical systems, robotics, or physical AI Evidence of leading funded projects and multidisciplinary research teams Experience mentoring junior faculty and student researchers Commitment to equity, sustainability, and community-engaged scholarship, and to teaching a diverse student body A collaborative, team-oriented approach suited to building and leading an interdisciplinary research cluster COMPENSATION Assistant Professor: $89,777 - $112,841 Associate Professor: $109,519 – $133,558 Full Professor: $130,755 – $160,827 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Only applications submitted through CUNYfirst will be considered for this position. If you are viewing this job posting in CUNYfirst, please click on \"Apply Now\" on the bottom of this page and follow the instructions. If you are viewing this job posting externally, please apply as follows: Go to https://cuny.jobs/ Search for Job Opening ID number 32771 Click on the \"Apply Now\" button and follow the instructions. Applications, including the following must be uploaded to the CUNYfirst job application website as a single PDF document: Cover letter explaining interest in the position and qualifications (including notable accomplishments in design and research), research agenda, and teaching philosophy (maximum 3 pages); Curriculum Vitae, including a publication list; A sample course syllabus; Two sample publications (no more than 50 pages); Digital portfolio of representative research, design work, and teaching (maximum 10 MB); Names and contact information of three (3) professional academic references, noting your relationship to each one. CLOSING DATE November 15, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32771 Location: City College of New York Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/assistant-professor-in-childhood-special-educationbilingual-education-tenure-track/E71E5B0E28BA4FC08F12F33F339D27FA/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Childhood Special Education/Bilingual Education (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Childhood Special Education/Bilingual Education (Tenure-Track) | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor in Childhood Special Education/Bilingual Education (Tenure-Track) New York, NY CITY COLLEGE OF NEW YORK Apply Now Assistant Professor in Childhood Special Education/Bilingual Education (Tenure-Track) FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT Position Details The Department of Interdisciplinary Arts & Sciences at the City College Center for Worker Education (CUNY) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Childhood Special Education/Bilingual Education, beginning in Fall 2027. Candidates should demonstrate active engagement in research, teaching, and community service, and be able to prepare early childhood educators and teach methods courses in early childhood special education and early childhood bilingual education. The successful candidate will also demonstrate enthusiasm and ability to collaborate across divisions and programs within City College. The department offers an interdisciplinary BA in Liberal Arts, a BA in Social Justice and Urban Life, a BS in Early Childhood Education for working adults, an MA in the Study of the Americas, and two new MA programs in Instructional Design and International and Global Education. The BS degree is offered jointly with the City College School of Education. The position will involve participation in some School of Education meetings, as well as data collection and analysis for accreditation bodies. Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach 4–5 courses (18 credit hours) per academic year. Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students. Work with MA students and contribute to the development of a growing curriculum in Early Childhood Education, International and Global Education, and Instructional Design. Build and sustain community partnerships. Engage in research and scholarly activities in areas of expertise. Share responsibility for departmental and college committee service. Perform administrative and supervisory duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. or Ed.D in a relevant field or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Preferred Qualifications Availability to work evening and weekend hours. Experience working full-time with children from birth through 2nd grade. Experience teaching in special education and bilingual education programs. Ability to teach successfully in an urban setting. Ph.D. or Ed.D. with specialization in Early Childhood Education, Special Education, or Bilingual Education. Commitment to teacher education, with a demonstrated record of scholarship and an active research agenda. Experience in applying contemporary adult education practices, innovative teaching modalities, and instructional technologies is especially encouraged. COMPENSATION Salary Range: $79,630 - $94,017 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Only applications submitted through CUNYfirst will be considered for this position. If you are viewing this job posting in CUNYfirst, please click on \"Apply Now\" on the bottom of this page and follow the instructions. If you are viewing this job posting externally, please apply as follows: Go to https://cuny.jobs/ Search for Job Opening ID number 32776 Click on the \"Apply Now\" button and follow the instructions. Applications, including the following must be uploaded to the CUNYfirst job application website as a single PDF document: Statement of scholarly interests; Curriculum Vitae / Resume; Names and contact information for three professional references CLOSING DATE November 15, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32776 Location: City College of New York Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/queens-ny/assistant-professor-applied-physiology/FF51CFD0F0F6454BB4CF9B46728A5BAB/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Jobs | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor - Applied Physiology Queens, NY QUEENSBOROUGH CC Apply Now Assistant Professor - Applied Physiology FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT The Department of Biological Sciences and Geology invites applications for the tenure track position of Assistant Professor in Applied Physiology starting in Spring 2027. The candidate will perform teaching, research and guidance duties in area(s) of expertise and will share responsibility for committee and department assignments including administrative, supervisory, and other functions as may be assigned. The successful candidate will teach courses in Anatomy and Physiology, Kinesiology, and Neurophysiology for majors. Duties include teaching, mentoring, advising undergraduates, maintaining scholarly activities including training undergraduate research students, and participating in department and college activities. Service includes serving on various committees like Assessment, Course and Standing, and Curriculum development. The candidate on this Assistant Professor line is expected to excel in teaching through the use of evidence-based pedagogy, demonstrate the ability to engage in scholarly research activities that result in publishable work, and provide service to the Department and College. The Department of Biological Sciences and Geology offers programs of study in Health Sciences, Biology, Public Health, Environmental Sciences, Medical Assistant, Biotechnology, Pre-Professional Studies, Pre-Nursing Curriculum, Geology, as well as required biology courses in Massage Therapy. The department's facilities include 15 state-of-the-art laboratories equipped with multimedia projection systems, two dedicated research laboratories, and a core facility with modern instrumentation. The department provides opportunities for professional growth, pedagogical development, and research. CUNY is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to increasing the diversity of its workforce. It welcomes nominations of, and applications from members of protected groups including minorities, women, veterans and individuals with disabilities, as well as others who would bring additional perspectives to the university’s mission. Candidates with demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusiveness through their teaching and/or service are also encouraged to apply. One of Queensborough Community College’s greatest strengths, and a necessary element of excellence, is the diversity of our community. We strive to attract and nurture a talented and diverse faculty and staff that proudly reflect the unique character of the local Queens community, the most diverse county in the United States. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. or Ed.D. degree in area(s) of Applied Physiology or a related field or a relevant professional doctorate, such as Doctor of Chiropractic. Candidates must have the required degree conferred by the time they submit their application. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS One or more years of prior teaching experience with effective evidence-based pedagogical practices. Experience in teaching entry level Anatomy and Physiology or Kinesiology, with ability to also teach Neurophysiology to science majors at an undergraduate institution. Demonstrate ability or potential to develop and sustain a program of scholarly research and to publish. Experience mentoring/advising students. Experience in teaching diverse student populations. COMPENSATION Salary Range $89,777-$98,231. Commensurate with experience and qualifications. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title.  Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must submit the following materials as a single PDF file : 1) a one-page cover letter; 2) a CV/resume; 3) a one-page statement of teaching philosophy; 4) a one-page statement of research plan and 5) names and contact information of three professional references. Candidates who earned their degree(s) outside the United States must provide a course-by-course evaluation from a recognized credential evaluation service verifying the U.S. equivalency of the degree. The evaluation must be submitted by the application deadline. CLOSING DATE October 7, 2026. Review of resumes to begin immediately. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32792 Location: Queensborough CC Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/queens-ny/asstistant-professor-general-biologymicrobiology/02FD7A2CCEE54CF591CC08D2EC65BACE/job/": {
      "title": "Asstistant Professor",
      "description": "Asstistant Professor - General Biology/Microbiology | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Asstistant Professor - General Biology/Microbiology Queens, NY QUEENSBOROUGH CC Apply Now Asstistant Professor - General Biology/Microbiology FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT The Department of Biological Sciences and Geology invites applications for the tenure track position of Assistant Professor in General Biology and/or Microbiology. The candidate will perform teaching, research and guidance duties in area(s) of expertise and will share responsibility for committee and department assignments including administrative, supervisory, and other functions as may be assigned. The successful candidate will teach courses in Microbiology and General Biology (with expertise in organismal biology, evolution, and biodiversity). Duties include teaching, mentoring and advising undergraduates, maintaining scholarly activities, including training undergraduate research students, and participating in Department as well as College activities. Service is expected in various committees such as Assessment, Course and Standing, and Curriculum development. The candidate on this Assistant Professor line will be expected to excel in teaching and using evidence-based pedagogy in the classroom, demonstrate the ability to engage in scholarly research activities that result in publishable work, and provide service to the Department and College. The Department of Biological Sciences and Geology offers programs of study in Health Sciences, Biology, Public Health, Environmental Sciences, Medical Assistant, Biotechnology, Pre-Professional Studies, Pre-Nursing Curriculum, Geology, as well as required biology courses in Massage Therapy. The department's facilities include 15 state-of-the-art laboratories equipped with multimedia projection systems, two dedicated research laboratories, and a core facility with modern instrumentation. The Department provides opportunities for professional growth, pedagogical development, and research. CUNY is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to increasing the diversity of its workforce. It welcomes nominations of, and applications from members of protected groups including minorities, women, veterans and individuals with disabilities, as well as others who would bring additional perspectives to the university’s mission. Candidates with demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusiveness through their teaching and/or service are also encouraged to apply. One of Queensborough Community College’s greatest strengths, and a necessary element of excellence, is the diversity of our community. We strive to attract and nurture a talented and diverse faculty and staff that proudly reflect the unique character of the local Queens community, the most diverse county in the United States. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Microbiology, Molecular Biology or related field. Candidates must have the required degree conferred by the time they submit their application. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS One or more years of prior teaching experience with effective evidence-based pedagogical practices. Experience in teaching entry-level General Biology (with expertise in organismal biology, evolution and biodiversity), and/or Microbiology to science majors. Demonstrated ability or potential to develop and sustain a program of scholarly research and to publish. Experience mentoring/advising students. Experience working with diverse student populations. COMPENSATION Salary Range $89,777-$98,231. Commensurate with experience and qualifications. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title.  Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must provide the following material in a single PDF: 1) a one-page cover letter; 2) a CV/resume; 3) a one-page statement of teaching philosophy; 4) a one-page statement of research plan; 5) the names and contact information of three professional references. Candidates who earned their degree(s) outside the United States must provide a course-by-course evaluation from a recognized credential evaluation service verifying the U.S. equivalency of the degree. The evaluation must be submitted by the application deadline. CLOSING DATE October 7, 2026. Review of resumes to begin immediately. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32791 Location: Queensborough CC Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
