    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/assistant-professor-tenure-track-architectural-history-and-urban-studies/9A030FF2474C49068AF5EE4CFF753DF6/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure-track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure-track) – Architectural History and Urban Studies | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor (Tenure-track) – Architectural History and Urban Studies New York, NY CITY COLLEGE OF NEW YORK Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-track) – Architectural History and Urban Studies FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT The Bernard and Anne Spitzer School of Architecture (SSA) seeks applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in architectural history and urban studies at the entering rank of assistant professor, starting Fall 2027. The candidates’ research and teaching will focus on the 20th and 21st centuries, and situate architectural history, urban history, and urban studies in global, transregional, and/or cross-cultural contexts. The successful candidate will teach in our B.A. in Urban Studies and the Built Environment program, offering the required lecture courses Introduction to Urban Studies and the City in History, and advise majors in a required two-semester capstone project. The successful candidate will also teach a global history of 20th- and 21st-century architecture in the SSA’s professional Bachelor and Master of Architecture programs. The faculty member will have the opportunity to teach advanced seminars in the area of specialization. The SSA is committed to social and sustainable concerns in design and practice, as well as to providing access to the finest education in the art, history, and technology of architecture, landscape architecture, urban design, and urban studies to the broadest and most diverse student population. A prospective member of the faculty should be prepared to participate in and contribute to this lively intellectual atmosphere, and join the SSA in its commitment in furthering justice, equity, diversity, inclusion, and anti-racism within the academy and the design professions. The Assistant Professor will share responsibility for committee and department assignments including administrative, supervisory, and other functions. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. degree in architectural history, urban history or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Preferred Qualifications Conferral of the Ph.D. is required before the start date in late August 2027. The candidate must have experience in teaching undergraduate and/or graduate lecture courses and seminars in architectural history and/or urban studies. Scholarship appropriate for an appointment at the rank of assistant professor. A deep commitment to city life and the fundamental principles of a public institution of higher education with a highly diverse student body is expected. COMPENSATION Salary Range: $89,777 - $112,841. Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Only applications submitted through CUNYfirst will be considered for this position. If you are viewing this job posting in CUNYfirst, please click on \"Apply Now\" on the bottom of this page and follow the instructions. If you are viewing this job posting externally, please apply as follows: Go to https://cuny.jobs/ Search for Job Opening ID number 32784 Click on the \"Apply Now\" button and follow the instructions. Applications, including the following must be uploaded to the CUNYfirst job application website as a single PDF document: Curriculum Vitae; Cover Letter explaining interest in position, teaching philosophy, and scholarly objectives. Candidates completing the Ph.D. at the time of application should specify the dates of their doctoral dissertation defense and degree conferral; One sample course syllabus; Two sample publications (50 pp. maximum in total); The names and contact information for three (3) professional academic references. CLOSING DATE November 24, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32784 Location: City College of New York Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sex